==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*pereh}}, probably derived from {{m|fiu-fin-pro|*perä||rear}}, referring to the background of a person (compare {{m|fi|alkuperä||origin}}, {{m|fi|peräisin||originating from}}, {{m|fi|perehtyä}}). First written appearance is from 1548 in the Finnish version of Sweden's {{m|fi|maanlaki||law of the country}} translated by a cleric known as {{w|lang=fi|Herra Martti}}.

Cognate with {{cog|et|pere}}, {{cog|krl|pereh}}, {{cog|liv|perē}}, {{cog|vep|pereh}} and {{cog|vro|pereh}}.

